      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "### ESLint version\n\n10.7.0\n\n### What problem do you want to solve?\n\nThe `-c, --config` help text currently reads:\n\n> Use this configuration instead of eslint.config.js, eslint.config.mjs, or eslint.config.cjs\n\nHowever, ESLint also supports TypeScript configuration files (`eslint.config.ts`, `eslint.config.mts`, and `eslint.config.cts`), so the current list is incomplete.\n\nThe [Command Line Interface documentation](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/command-line-interface#options) embeds the CLI help output and therefore displays the same incomplete description.\n\nThis came up while updating the configuration filename patterns in the glossary [#21095](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/21095#discussion_r3610849246):\n\n### What do you think is the correct solution?\n\nUpdate the description in [`lib/options.js`](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/main/lib/options.js#L100) to account for the TypeScript configuration file names, then regenerate the CLI documentation so that it matches the updated help output.\n\nA couple of wording details may need discussion:\n\n* Listing all six filenames would make the help text fairly long. Alternatives could include mentioning only `eslint.config.js` followed by \"or another supported flat config file format,\" or using a more compact filename pattern.\n* The documentation notes that [TypeScript configuration files require additional setup](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/configure/configuration-files#typescript-configuration-files), so the wording should avoid implying that they work out of the box.\n\nI\u2019m happy to use whichever wording the team prefers.\n\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this change.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\n_No response_",
